{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood","id":634611,"title":"[2ED] Power(s) of Blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-21T08:26:35-07:00","id":634611,"title":"[2ED] Power(s) of Blood","content":"As I'm going to run crossover game of <b>Beast</b> &amp; <b>Vampire</b>, I have some questions. First - <b>Can non-ghouled mortal be still under Healing by the Blood? Or does he need to be made in to ghoul so the Vitea would work?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T08:49:12-07:00","id":634635,"title":"","content":"It is just for ghouls. Difficult to say the effect of house ruling otherwise. Why would you not want to ghoul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:40:22-07:00","id":634839,"title":"","content":"Technically, you need to ghoul someone, but there's no reason you can't change it. I rule that vmapire blood can also be used as tass in Mage, for instance<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:59:08-07:00","id":634856,"title":"","content":"In<b> Beast</b> corebook SAS <i>&quot;Morning After&quot;</i> there is scene where the PCs can save mans life - only not the Begotten, but other supernaturals. I concluded that vampires could give him their Blood to heal his deadly wounds. But mine Kindred players could resist to take unhooked mortal to their Requiem, especially as two Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum Daeva. I just make sure if the mortal can be healed with Blood without making him ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:47:28-07:00","id":634915,"title":"","content":"A ghoul doesn't need to know they are a ghoul. The Deprived condition would go away eventually. I think you can split things by keeping the willpower cost to ghoul and allow ghoul healing while losing the breaking point and other benefits and drawbacks of ghouldom. Allowing Vitae to heal without added cost means people can hunt vampires for their healing blood. Sounds dangerous to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T21:21:05-07:00","id":635427,"title":"","content":"Other question - <b>Did there be set effect on Kindred drinking blood from the Beasts?</b> I would suspect something like hallucination trip of mages and changelings, but in imaginary of Beast's Horror and it's Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T01:08:36-07:00","id":635500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=634915#post634915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)The Deprived condition would go away eventually. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? According to my understanding of the new rules, ghouls are now permanently ghouls and cannot become human again (with the exception of special powers, blood magic, etc). Also, for me it would not fit thematically if a vampire could heal a human without any drawbacks for the victim. So, I would'nt allow it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T04:59:03-07:00","id":635604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=634856#post634856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In<b> Beast</b> corebook SAS <i>&quot;Morning After&quot;</i> there is scene where the PCs can save mans life - only not the Begotten, but other supernaturals. I concluded that vampires could give him their Blood to heal his deadly wounds. But mine Kindred players could resist to take unhooked mortal to their Requiem, especially as two Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum Daeva. I just make sure if the mortal can be healed with Blood without making him ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then... ghoul the guy, dominate him to make him forget the vamps and the blood, and walk away? That's a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=634915#post634915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghoul doesn't need to know they are a ghoul. The Deprived condition would go away eventually. I think you can split things by keeping the willpower cost to ghoul and allow ghoul healing while losing the breaking point and other benefits and drawbacks of ghouldom. Allowing Vitae to heal without added cost means people can hunt vampires for their healing blood. Sounds dangerous to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like an awesome plot hook to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=635500#post635500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it? According to my understanding of the new rules, ghouls are now permanently ghouls and cannot become human again (with the exception of special powers, blood magic, etc). Also, for me it would not fit thematically if a vampire could heal a human without any drawbacks for the victim. So, I would'nt allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, there is a drawback - the vampire is losing blood, and the victim is addicted and has to go through withdraw.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen anything in the new rules that would suggest they cannot stop being a ghoul. I see lines from the core book like, &quot;Except none of it\u2019s really yours. Miss a dose, and the train rushing through your veins derails. The withdrawal\u2019s bad, so bad. But there\u2019s something worse. All of a sudden, with just a missed taste of Vitae\u2026 you\u2019re normal. Mundane. Prole. Rat in a cage.&quot; This suggests becoming mortal again.<br /> <br /> Sure, you still have access to the old supernatural stuff if you Resolve your Depraved Condition. You're not reghouled and starting over. But, for all intents and purposes, you have the biology and abilities of a mortal. And, yes, Conditions do expire without being Resolved and just fade away. If this one didn't, it would say that it was a Persistant Depraved Condition. It doesn't. It specifically lacks a (Persistant) tag, so by the rules it does expire with time.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-22-2015, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T06:09:56-07:00","id":635713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=635604#post635604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, there is a drawback - the vampire is losing blood, and the victim is addicted and has to go through withdraw.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this price is much too low for the ability to heal a human back to normal from the brink of death. But it depends on how harshly the vitae addiction is played out, if it is like a drug such as heroine, then maybe it is punishing enough to feel right. Still, by the rules, I don't think it is intended that a human can be healed with blood. Ghouls use the vitae &quot;stored&quot; within them to heal themselves. Humans lack this ability, and a vampire cannot spend vitae &quot;in place of&quot; someone else without a proper discipline or devotion to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't seen anything in the new rules that would suggest they cannot stop being a ghoul. I see lines from the core book like, &quot;Except none of it\u2019s really yours. Miss a dose, and the train rushing through your veins derails. The withdrawal\u2019s bad, so bad. But there\u2019s something worse. All of a sudden, with just a missed taste of Vitae\u2026 you\u2019re normal. Mundane. Prole. Rat in a cage.&quot; This suggests becoming mortal again.<br /> <br /> Sure, you still have access to the old supernatural stuff if you Resolve your Depraved Condition. You're not reghouled and starting over. But, for all intents and purposes, you have the biology and abilities of a mortal. And, yes, Conditions do expire without being Resolved and just fade away. If this one didn't, it would say that it was a Persistant Depraved Condition. It doesn't. It specifically lacks a (Persistant) tag, so by the rules it does expire with time. </div> </div> </div>The rules are not very clear in this point, I hope the forthcoming half-damned book will treat this in more detail. I would actually really like if there is no coming back from being a ghoul. Endless deprivation seems like a fitting fate for a ghoul. There can be different interpretations, but for me a powerless ghoul is still a ghoul.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1125,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","user":"gflash","date":". 08-22-2015, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T06:47:36-07:00","id":635726,"title":"","content":"The plot hook is why I question the decision to try to avoid ghouling. The withdrawal won't end until the necessary vitae is imbibed, but the Deprived condition would end with time. If a ghoul knows what is going on then they would still act like a junkie given a chance at some vitae. I think a ghoul in withdrawal that makes it through deprivation <i>should</i> be able to function as a normal person. It works for drug addicts. Whether a ghoul in withdrawal is still a ghoul seems like semantics to me.<br /> <br /> For feeding from a Beast, I think the Frightened Condition or maybe even the Delusional Condition (if you want to be nasty) would be the easy way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-22-2015, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:18:35-07:00","id":635819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=635427#post635427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other question - <b>Did there be set effect on Kindred drinking blood from the Beasts?</b> I would suspect something like hallucination trip of mages and changelings, but in imaginary of Beast's Horror and it's Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div> First, let me point out that, in 2e, there's no official set disadvantage (because they're always disadvantages). The only requirement in 2e is that you need the merit.<br /> <br /> If you absolutely must have a penalty, then you're better off either 1) making the vampire hungry to feed more or establish social dominance (inflict the supernatural hungers that would count as Family Dinner), or 2) inflict an anathema. The thing about supernatural vitae drawbacks in 1e is that they are always the drawback of the supernatural in question. Werewolf blood makes you prone to rages. Mage blood inflicts paradox-bedlam-like madness. Changeling blood makes you unable to tell fantasy from reality. Promethean blood gives you Disquiet. So, if you want to keep that up, I'd go with something that's a &quot;weakness&quot; of Beasts.<br /> <br /> I also recommend converting it into the form of a Condition. Make it an incentive.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:34:06-07:00","id":635823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=635713#post635713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this price is much too low for the ability to heal a human back to normal from the brink of death.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It might save them, but it's not like it's instant or cheap. Any aggravated damage takes two nights and five vitae. It's not like you can just force feed a human a little blood and they're right as rain in a few minutes or even hours. Lethal is 1:1, and bashing is 2:1. Ghouls can only even hold Vitae = Stamina dots, so the vampire will have to be there feeding them Vitae pretty constantly, and most vampires can only carry between 10 and 20 Vitae, some of which they need for themselves.<br /> <br /> Healing a human back from the brink of death is incredibly difficult and costly for a vampire even using Ghouling. If there's aggravated damage involved, you're probably also talking about a stage 3 blood bond very quickly, and I don't interpret those as universally beneficial for the vampire like some people do. It's an obsession, and that can be unpredictable and something a vampire doesn't want.<br /> <br /> Stabilizing them is easier, but you can do that with a single mundane dice roll anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T12:40:49-07:00","id":636189,"title":"","content":"The direct answers, by RAW, are:<br /> <br /> 1- No. The mortal have to be Ghouled;<br /> <br /> 2- No, there are no set rules.<br /> <br /> Both can be easily house-ruled for your convenience. I would go with Conditions for the second one, by the way, be them good or bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T16:45:43-07:00","id":636430,"title":"","content":"So can other people tap vampires to make healing potions? Just stake 'em, stick a spigot in them and fill up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-22-2015, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T18:26:30-07:00","id":636521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=636430#post636430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can other people tap vampires to make healing potions? Just stake 'em, stick a spigot in them and fill up?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be why I suggested it might cause problems not to ghoul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T21:58:45-07:00","id":636682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=635823#post635823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might save them, but it's not like it's instant or cheap. Any aggravated damage takes two nights and five vitae. It's not like you can just force feed a human a little blood and they're right as rain in a few minutes or even hours. Lethal is 1:1, and bashing is 2:1. Ghouls can only even hold Vitae = Stamina dots, so the vampire will have to be there feeding them Vitae pretty constantly, and most vampires can only carry between 10 and 20 Vitae, some of which they need for themselves.<br /> <br /> Healing a human back from the brink of death is incredibly difficult and costly for a vampire even using Ghouling. If there's aggravated damage involved, you're probably also talking about a stage 3 blood bond very quickly, and I don't interpret those as universally beneficial for the vampire like some people do. It's an obsession, and that can be unpredictable and something a vampire doesn't want.<br /> <br /> Stabilizing them is easier, but you can do that with a single mundane dice roll anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I also think that drinking Vitea for instant healing is enough. Healing is one thing, making another person permanent Ghoul connected to you as Regent is totally different level of matter. Also, this lead to second thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/634611-2ed-power-s-of-blood?p=636430#post636430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can other people tap vampires to make healing potions? Just stake 'em, stick a spigot in them and fill up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally okay with this - in-story reasons ( i.e. mortals hunting for vampires ) makes thing leading to vampire making ghouls or at least Blood Bonded their mortals they give Blood. But in some examples Kindred can save his mortal friends life - only he started a Blood Bond on him, so even if player did not wanted to ghoul friend before, things will escalate quickly, in story tells. Instant plot line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}